Interview Preparation Checklist

By the end of your learning, you should be able to confidently answer:

	100+ Ansible interview questions
	50+ production troubleshooting scenarios
	30+ role-based automation examples
	20+ Vault and security questions
	15+ CI/CD integration questions
	10+ performance optimization questions
	5+ architecture and design discussions
	My recommendation for your background

Given your experience, I'd prioritize topics in this order:

	Roles & reusable project structure
	Variables, facts, and Jinja2
	Execution control and error handling
	Vault and security
	Jenkins + GitHub Actions integration
	AWS dynamic inventory
	AWX / Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform
	Performance optimization (1000+ servers)
	Custom modules and plugins (Python)
	Real enterprise deployment patterns (Blue-Green, Canary, Rolling)